{
  "title": "Web: collapse CookbookPage's 4 copy-pasted bulk-AI handlers into \
one helper; stop using the error signal for success messages",
  "description": "ramekin-ui/src/pages/CookbookPage.tsx:747-886 — \
bulkNormalizeTitle, bulkGenerateDescription, bulkGeneratePhoto, \
bulkRescrapePhoto are ~35-line copies of the same shape (confirm -> set \
progress -> per-id loop with try/catch/extractApiError -> aggregate errors -> \
final message), backed by 4 identical progress signals at :288-303. They \
differ only in API call, confirm text, and success wording.\n\
\n\
Fix: one runBulkOperation({ ids, action, confirm, summarize }) helper and a \
single progress signal.\n\
\n\
Related: the error signal is overloaded to carry success messages — :774-782, \
:812-820, :848-854 call setError(\"Normalized N recipes...\") etc. on the \
success path, so success feedback renders in the error UI and can't be styled \
or cleared distinctly. Add a separate status/notice signal (or a shared \
toast).\n\
\n\
Web-only UI refactor; iOS has no equivalent bulk UI today.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
